A site whose Autoplay is Block, or any site without its own setting while Block autoplay everywhere is on, plays
media only after its user asked, enforced in Blink rather than in the page's world. The Mac port of
scripts/windows/engine/patches/chromium-win-autoplay-policy.patch: ArdiaCore (ac_autoplay.cc) decides from the tab's
top-level origin and sends it with each commit and on live changes (ACPage SetAutoplayBlocked); Ardia's media
control marks its frame's document asked (ACPage NoteMediaCommand). No refusal count is reported. Web Audio, which
the Windows patch leaves out, follows the same answer: an AudioContext doesn't start, resume, start from a source node
or come back from an interruption until its document's user asked, and one running when the answer turns to Block is
suspended; a resume() that was already completing then leaves it suspended, with its promise pending.

